infographic list-column-simple-vertical-arrow
data
  title Injection scopes: how many instances live
  desc From one cached app-wide singleton to a fresh instance per request
  lists
    - label Scope.DEFAULT — one instance app-wide
      desc Singleton built once at boot and cached. The fast norm: no per-request allocation, the graph is already wired.
    - label Scope.TRANSIENT — one instance per consumer
      desc A fresh, unshared instance for each injector. For per-consumer stateful helpers like a logger with its own context.
    - label Scope.REQUEST — one instance per request
      desc New instance each request, GC'd when it ends — and contagious: it bubbles UP the chain, making every consumer request-scoped.
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f59e0b #f43f5e
